# Extra jpackage options for Linux, passed as @packaging/linux/jpackage.args.
#
# No shortcut option: the .deb already installs a menu entry, because jpackage registers the
# Modula.desktop template it finds in this directory (checked: 1.2.0's postinst runs
# xdg-desktop-menu install on it).
#
# No --license-file: it pastes LICENSE under "License:" as it stands, so the deb's copyright read
# "License: MIT License" and was not machine-readable. scripts/finish-deb.sh writes a proper one.
#
# The deb's Homepage, and the only part of the listing GNOME Software's window for a downloaded
# .deb shows besides the description: it reads the package's own fields and nothing else. Must
# equal modula.homepage in the pom (PackagingTest).
--about-url
https://github.com/adriandeleon/Modula
# Without it the Maintainer field reads "Adrian De Leon <Unknown>".
--linux-deb-maintainer
adrian.deleon@gmail.com
# Debian's own section for radio software, in place of jpackage's "misc".
--linux-app-category
hamradio
